+| Surface ack and resync (3b) | c→s `EndpointControl{x-mosh.surface-ack.v1 / x-mosh.surface-resync.v1}`, JSON. Welcome capability `x-mosh-surface-ack`. The client opts in implicitly by sending its first ack | No. All four codecs and `PaneSurfacePatch` already carry `base_surface_revision`. **The semantic change** is that the relaxed `new > base` (`surface_reuse.rs:62`, `surface_patch.rs:120`) and older retained bases become legal. That only happens after negotiation and the first ack. A new client talking to an old server keeps fatal-desync behaviour, because the old server silently ignores unknown kinds at `client_transport.rs:1349-1354` and the client would otherwise wait forever |
+| RTT hint (2-fallback) | keeper→server `x-mosh.link.rtt.v1` | No |
+| QUIC (3) | Bridge-internal ALPN `herdr-bridge/1`, token, channel header and offset stamp. The herdr frame stream is carried byte for byte | No |
+| Echo ack and input marks (4) | s→c `x-mosh.echo-ack.v1` appended to the render-lane item; c→s `x-mosh.input-mark.v1` | No. Never put it in `PaneSurfacePatch`/`Frame` metadata. Those are frozen bincode structs, so the plan's wording "stamp into surface metadata" (`mosh-like-herdr-plan.md:22`; report §8) would break the wire |
